1
00:00:00,550 --> 00:00:02,428
AI is moving out of the cloud

2
00:00:02,428 --> 00:00:04,177
and onto your own computer.

3
00:00:04,709 --> 00:00:05,459
Private.

4
00:00:05,725 --> 00:00:06,535
Private. Offline.

5
00:00:06,801 --> 00:00:07,561
Private. Offline. Yours.

6
00:00:08,092 --> 00:00:10,192
But the electric bill is yours too.

7
00:00:11,895 --> 00:00:14,113
How much power does your AI really use?

8
00:00:14,645 --> 00:00:16,150
Most tools just guess.

9
00:00:17,001 --> 00:00:18,260
Meet WattTrace.

10
00:00:18,792 --> 00:00:20,733
It runs entirely on your machine.

11
00:00:21,265 --> 00:00:24,081
No cloud, no account, no extra hardware.

12
00:00:24,932 --> 00:00:26,566
Every two seconds, it reads

13
00:00:26,566 --> 00:00:28,623
your computer's own power sensors.

14
00:00:29,155 --> 00:00:31,203
That total is measured, not guessed.

15
00:00:31,735 --> 00:00:35,132
Then it splits that power between your AI apps,

16
00:00:35,132 --> 00:00:37,879
by how much CPU and GPU each one uses.

17
00:00:38,411 --> 00:00:40,849
Anything without a sensor is estimated,

18
00:00:40,849 --> 00:00:42,037
and always labeled.

19
00:00:42,569 --> 00:00:44,930
And you can check it against a wall meter.

20
00:00:45,781 --> 00:00:49,088
Watts become kilowatt-hours, pesos, and carbon.

21
00:00:49,620 --> 00:00:51,777
It forecasts your bill, and one click

22
00:00:51,777 --> 00:00:53,993
swaps a heavy model for a lighter one.

23
00:00:54,844 --> 00:00:57,125
WattTrace. Measured, not guessed.

24
00:00:57,125 --> 00:00:58,300
Local, not cloud.

